\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   Rise up all ye people on earth,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Look into the heavens!
\par  see the morning star appearing
\par  Pointing towards Jesus.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.   This is the star of Bethlehem,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Showing our Lord has come
\par  pointing exactly where he lay,
\par  for  people to worship.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.   This is not a star which is lost:
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Let us all follow it!
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   It will lead onward to Jesus,
\par   and we shall reach Him too.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  All you that are in darkness still
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   A light is shinning up.
\par   This dozing world shall be awake,
\par   and the blind men shall see.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  O! master let us recognize
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   the world's light that you are
\par   Let us befilled with your true love
\par \pard       as children of the light.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

